@@ -13,17 +13,51 @@ Implements the `gpui::Platform` trait for mobile targets, following the same arc
 | **iOS** | Metal via wgpu | CoreText |
 | **Android** | Vulkan/GL via wgpu | cosmic-text + swash |
 
-**Highlights:** GPU-accelerated rendering, touch input with momentum scrolling, keyboard support, safe area insets, dark mode, and emoji rendering.
+**Highlights:** GPU-accelerated rendering, touch input with momentum scrolling, keyboard support, safe-area and IME insets through GPUI's `PlatformWindow` API, dark mode, and emoji rendering. Android IME inset delivery uses `GpuiInputActivity` and Android `WindowInsets` (with animated updates on API 30+ and a visible-frame fallback on older supported Android versions); custom hosts must forward those insets to the native bridge. Native VoiceOver/TalkBack accessibility-tree integration is not implemented yet.
 
 ## Custom Android hosts
 
 Custom Android hosts should extend `dev.gpui.mobile.GpuiInputActivity` instead of
 `android.app.NativeActivity` to receive multistage IME composition through a
-native `InputConnection`. Include `GpuiInputActivity.java` and retain the usual
-`android.app.lib_name` metadata. For GPUI file prompts, also package
+native `InputConnection`. Add this repository's Gradle Android library as a
+source project dependency; the Java runtime glue lives in `gpui-mobile/android`
+and should not be copied into the app. For example, from an app's Gradle
+settings file:
+
+```kotlin
+include(":gpui-mobile")
+project(":gpui-mobile").projectDir = file("<path-to-gpui-mobile>/android")
+```
+
+Then add `implementation(project(":gpui-mobile"))` to the app module. The app
+must use `compileSdk` 36 or newer and declare its concrete launch Activity in
+its own manifest, including the `android.app.lib_name` metadata naming the Rust
+shared library, `android:configChanges` for handled orientation/screen/keyboard
+changes, and `android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"`. The library manifest
+intentionally declares no app ID, launch Activity, or native library name. For
+GPUI file prompts, also package
 `GpuiPathPicker.java` and register its non-exported Activity as shown in the
 example manifest. The picker imports documents into app cache before returning
-filesystem paths; it does not require broad storage permissions.
+filesystem paths; it does not require broad storage permissions. Save-dialog
+requests are explicitly unsupported on Android and return an error.
+
+**Android session ownership:** each `NativeActivity` gets a new platform/App
+session. Teardown cancels the QuickJS owner, retires GPUI callbacks on the loop
+thread, shuts down foreground dispatch, releases the session GPU device and
+uninstalls the acquired main-looper reference. Surface-bound GPU resources are
+released **before** acknowledging `TerminateWindow`; the raw window wrapper
+retains its `ANativeWindow`. Background/resume rebuilds the surface while keeping
+the logical window and atlas handle. A lost vsync cannot indefinitely strand an
+owed frame; this bounded wait does not render idle windows continuously.
+
+The local QuickJS/Svelte fixture has passed two consecutive three-cycle runs
+(six Back/destroy/relaunch cycles) in one Android **emulator PID**, including new rendering and native input after
+each launch, independent bindings, HOME/resume, rotation and post-rotation input.
+Activity destruction starts a fresh app; HOME/resume and handled rotation retain
+its state. This is not physical-device or production-readiness validation. The
+repeatable harness is `gpuix-svelte/test/mobile-android/lifecycle.mjs` in the local
+frontend fork. IME coverage and remaining platform limitations must be reported
+separately from successful Activity recreation.
 
